# Expo env — copy to .env and edit.
#
# ── Local web dev (Chrome on the same Mac as the backend) ────────────
# LEAVE EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL COMMENTED OUT.
# The client at src/api/client.ts falls back to window.location.hostname,
# so http://localhost:8082 automatically fetches from
# http://localhost:8000/api. No IP editing required when your Wi-Fi
# changes networks.
#
# ── Phone on LAN pointed at the Mac ──────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment + set the Mac's current LAN IP. Run:
#   ifconfig | grep "inet " | grep -v 127.0.0.1
# to find it. Restart `npx expo start` after editing — env vars are
# only read at launch.
#
# ── Production / deployed backend ────────────────────────────────────
# Point at the deployed backend (Railway / Fly / Render / etc).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.cremabrews.com/api

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.0.101:8000/api
